 # Working notes: ea61d17502dd
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## Review repair: v3.0.0
+
+Pinned baseline generator SHA-256:
+`0ef9e4dee146770a6458aef7bea5688d5ae573f2dc8d22fd9de3b42e3782b608`.
+Final generator SHA-256:
+`14dd226548de92e9d3d900cc4ace5c1644687981ea467c5602e52a519649703c`.
+
+The unverified prior return `review-9d83cd0729c9e31b:v0001` was used only as a
+lead. Its invalid-value aliasing and inert-axis claims were reproduced against
+the pinned baseline before repair.
+
+### Repaired defects
+
+- Removed four advertised but inert controls and retained only exact,
+  reconstructible axes: grid height, grid width, crossing priority, and span
+  mode.
+- Reject unknown keys and invalid values instead of silently aliasing malformed
+  `primary` values to vertical.
+- Honor the full declared boundary range in every difficulty band.
+- Accept all canonical inputs, including partial strands and the 25x15 profile;
+  the old validator incorrectly required both strands to span the full grid.
+- Generate both canonical full-span and lawful partial-span crosses.
+- Add a deterministic four-profile semantic schedule so every consecutive
+  three-example window contains both horizontal and vertical priority.
+- Add a fail-closed structural analyzer, an exact Python rule mirror, witnesses,
+  two priority-blind rivals, and a lesson-level identifiability contract.
+- Synchronize the selected augmented Racket text with the selected training text.
+  Execution parity already passed; this was exact-source drift only, not a rule
+  semantic change.
+
+### Evidence
+
+The completed baseline battery was 5 green, 1 advisory, and 6 failed. The final
+battery is 12/12 green. Selected tests pass 73/73. The Racket-backed lesson census
+refutes both declared priority rivals in 300/300 production lessons (100 per
+band). The source-bound curriculum probe additionally checks 32 consecutive
+cyclic starts per band: 96/96 windows identifiable, 300/300 generated scenes
+strict-valid and deterministic, and all four `(primary, span_mode)` cells occur
+25 times per 100 draws in every band.
+
+### Domain limits
+
+The finite rivals establish resistance to the two named priority-blind rules,
+not universal induction. Inputs outside the documented 10..25 by 10..15,
+four-color, one-cross grammar are rejected. The output rule remains the selected
+canonical Racket authority; the Python mirror is test and probe support only.
+
+Imported associated notes remain in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
