-Keep alternate drafts, reproducers, and unfinished experiments here.
-The selected implementation is `../generator.py`. Workspace drafts are never automatically selected.
+`curriculum_probe.py` is a fast, source-bound regression census for the selected
+implementation in `../generator.py`. It measures strict validity, deterministic
+replay, input/output diversity, all four `(primary, span_mode)` schedule cells,
+priority-rival disagreement, and every sampled consecutive lesson window.
+
+It deliberately uses the Python rule mirror rather than Racket, so it is a cheap
+iteration tool, not final authority evidence. Final semantic evidence must still
+come from the shared Racket-backed battery and `lesson-census` command.
+
+Run from `repo/`:
+
+```bash
+python3 generators/ea61d17502dd/workspace/curriculum_probe.py \
+  --per-band 100 --lesson-starts 32 \
+  --out ../checks/curriculum-probe-final.json
+```
+
+With the four-step balanced schedule, each priority-blind rival is expected to
+disagree on half of the individual samples, while every complete three-example
+window must refute both rivals. A rival need only be refuted somewhere in the
+sample; requiring disagreement on every sample would incorrectly reject a
+well-formed conditional rival.
